      "name": null,
      "problem": "Express $\\frac{1}{81}$ as a base raised to a negative exponent.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write $\\frac{1}{81}$ as a base raised to a power:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{81} & =\\frac{1\\times 1}{9\\times 9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\times \\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the reciprocal of the base $(\\frac{1}{9}),$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the *opposite* sign $(-2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}={9}^{-2}\n$$",
